event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1192,"item_id":"fc_0cafbe3bbeb5c935016adb4ea6891c81918ef51cc89314061f","output_index":2,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"checks\":{\"source_route_and_coverage\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"R001 has the sole source output P and exact direct inputs H001–H004. T001 lists S001–S008 and its explanation tracks the source route: highest-weight basis and string termination, matrix units, arbitrary-lattice coordinate modules and rank-one generator, reduction and action matrices, then invariant-subspace argument. No standard-lattice replacement or new library proof route is proposed. This is a route/coverage judgment only, not proof-body validation.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/argument\"},{\"document\":\"source-map.json\",\"pointer\":\"/direct_boundaries/R001\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0\"}]},\"parameters_and_allowed_inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The contract retains p, K, lam, M and the D record with Nat.Prime p, CharP K p, 0 ≤ lam < p and exactly H001–H004 as T001 inputs. The Nat/Int encoding preserves the integer endpoint condition with the explicit guard; the Fin (lam.toNat + 1) basis fields are consequently guarded by nonnegativity. The contract does not specialize to a standard lattice or exclude p=2 or lam=0. H004 expands the source conditions into basis, embedding, bracket, highest-vector, integral-action and divided-power preservation data, and includes complex Lie irreducibility, all of which reflect stated source conditions; no extra target conclusion over K is included there. The instance/typeclass binders supply ambient algebraic structures, not an additional mathematical hypothesis.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"spec.json\",\"pointer\":\"/hypotheses\"},{\"document\":\"source-context.md\",\"pointer\":\"/42\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/inferences/0/inputs\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/parameters\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/premises\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/header\"},{\"document\":\"type-result.json\",\"pointer\":\"/stdout\"}]},\"representations_and_conversion_obligations\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The chosen lattice is arbitrary: D carries an integer module, basis, injective embedding into the complex module and compatible operators, rather than fixing a standard lattice. The target predicate correctly expresses nontriviality and the invariant-subspace condition, and the complex dividedPower matches the source divided powers. However the source output and S004/S005 identify M ⊗[ℤ] K, while the formal conclusion and T001 act on K ⊗[ℤ] M. The representation notes themselves acknowledge that the tensor commutor must be proved/used, but neither contract nor plan supplies a typed conversion obligation or lists it as an input/step. Its existence is a familiar conversion, not an interface fact supplied by elaboration; source/formal output correspondence therefore remains unestablished. There is also no explicit Lean realization of R, J_i/J or the rank-one argument, but that is acceptable as internal proof work under the single coarse T provided the eventual proof follows those paragraphs and proves the required transports.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/propositions/4\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/argument/3\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/conclusion\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/representation\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/header\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/representation_notes\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0\"}]},\"statements_and_local_plans\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"T001 is propositionally the formal contract conclusion and is conditional on the listed exact source inputs; it is not merely a renamed theorem, because its target predicate is a concrete definition of nontriviality and invariant subspaces. Its explanation is recognizably faithful to all eight source paragraphs, including the lambda=0 and characteristic-2 cases, and it does not claim a completed proof. But the terminal type proves irreducibility for K ⊗[ℤ] M, whereas source P is for M ⊗[ℤ] K. The explanation discusses the source module and its basis correspondence without stating a conversion theorem at the typed-plan level or an assembly obligation that transports the result. Thus the terminal statement is not yet a source-facing realization of P. The type-check receipt establishes elaboration only and cannot discharge this semantic discrepancy.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/propositions/4\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/argument/3\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/conclusion/type\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0/statement\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0/explanation\"},{\"document\":\"type-Check.lean\",\"pointer\":\"/37\"},{\"document\":\"type-result.json\",\"pointer\":\"/stdout\"}]}},\"findings\":[{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"explanation\":\"Unprovided source/formal tensor-order conversion: P and the source argument use M ⊗[ℤ] K, but the contract and terminal Lean proposition use K ⊗[ℤ] M. Although the representation notes acknowledge the need to prove/use the tensor commutor, no typed bridge or assembly conversion obligation appears in the plan. Hence equivalence of the source output and formal target is not established by the proposal or the type check.\",\"locations\":[{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/propositions/4\"},{\"document\":\"nl0.json\",\"pointer\":\"/argument/3\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/conclusion/type\"},{\"document\":\"contract.json\",\"pointer\":\"/representation\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0/statement\"},{\"document\":\"plan.json\",\"pointer\":\"/steps/0/inputs\"}]}]}}"}

